---
import PunctumLayout from "../../../layouts/PunctumLayout.astro";
---

<PunctumLayout
  title="About Punctum — A study of situated attention"
  description="A photographic experiment about the private details that catch and stay with us."
>
  <main class="punctum-about">
    <h1 class="punctum-about__title">
      We do not all see<br />the same <em>image.</em>
    </h1>
    <div class="punctum-about__grid">
      <aside class="punctum-about__index">
        Punctum<br />
        A study of<br />
        situated attention
      </aside>
      <div class="punctum-about__content">
        <section>
          <h2>The image changes.</h2>
          <p>
            A photograph does not carry one complete and permanent meaning.
            Its meaning changes with the person who encounters it.
          </p>
          <p>
            The same image may feel beautiful to one person, unsettling to
            another, and entirely ordinary to someone else.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>Attention is situated.</h2>
          <p>
            What pulls us towards an image is connected to what we already
            carry within us—memory, locality, culture, age, and circumstance.
          </p>
          <p>
            An image may be made by a photographer, but its meaning is also
            made by its viewers.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>A private response becomes a collective map.</h2>
          <p>
            Each participant contributes a drawn region and, optionally, a few
            words. Across many viewers, these responses form a visual archive
            of declared attention.
          </p>
          <p>
            The heatmap does not replace interpretation. It creates another way
            to begin it.
          </p>
          <a class="punctum-button punctum-button--yellow" href="/research/punctum/experiment">
            Lend your attention
          </a>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</PunctumLayout>
